{{!-- /the-faith-received/ask/ — the Ask workspace.

     WHAT THIS PAGE IS. Almost nothing. The corpus owner's engine
     (assets/js/port/ask-workspace.js) builds the entire surface itself
     and opens on boot; this template exists to load it inside Mere
     Orthodoxy's shell, give it our stylesheet instead of his, and hand
     it the two things it cannot work out for itself.

     SKIN AND BONES. His engine, our design. We deliberately do NOT
     load assets/css/port/ask-workspace.css: his pages carry a second
     masthead, two Google faces and a bridge bar back to his site, and
     dropped in whole they read as another publication living here.
     assets/css/faith-ask-workspace.css replaces it wholesale, keeping
     his class names because they are what his DOM emits.

     SCRIPT ORDER MATTERS, and not in the usual way. Page scripts in
     this theme run inside {{{body}}}, BEFORE site.min.js — so nothing
     here may depend on a site-bundle global. It depends on window.MOAuth
     instead, which ships in the BOOT bundle and is therefore already
     present. That is what mints the member bearer; see the MereO delta
     in ask-workspace.js and ask-worker.js.

     ask-store.js first: ask-workspace.js reads FRChatStore at boot.

     THE SHAREDWORKER. The stream is owned by a SharedWorker at
     /assets/js/port/ask-worker.js, which is why a question survives
     navigation and a closed tab. It is fetched by absolute path at
     runtime by the engine, so it must exist at exactly that path and
     must NOT be renamed or bundled.

     NOTHING ON THIS PAGE MAY BE AN INLINE SCRIPT. The theme's CSP is
     `script-src 'self'` with no 'unsafe-inline', so an inline <script>
     is refused and never runs. Three fixes for this page shipped inline
     and none executed. The open call lives in
     assets/js/page/faith-ask-open.js.

     WHY WE CALL open() OURSELVES. The engine opens on its own only when
     the path matches /ask, or when the URL carries ?ask= or ?m=ask.
     Ours is /the-faith-received/ask-workspace/, which matches none of
     them.

     It also reads a window.__FR_ASK_PENDING__ global at boot, and that
     is what this template used first. It does not work: verified on the
     live page, the global is set before the engine script loads and in
     the right order, the engine consumes it, and the workspace is still
     never built — while ?ask= on the same URL opens it every time. So
     the hook is not load-bearing here and we do not depend on it.

     Instead the engine is asked directly, once it exists. window.FRAsk
     is published synchronously by ask-workspace.js, so a script after it
     can call open() with no waiting and no polling. The isOpen() guard
     means a URL that ALSO carries ?ask= opens once, not twice. --}}

